root=Path.cwd();p=root/'docs/MUSIC_STUDIO.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s+='''\n\n## November 1 — tremble report and model research\nUser reports 50/70-step auditions sound the same and retain a trembling, non-continuous voice. Do not increase production steps based on this failed perceptual comparison. Local RMVPE traces saved under country-roads-consistency-20261101/pitch-diagnosis.json and pitch-traces.npz. The 70-step clip has lower fast-pitch residual than 50, close to the guide by this limited metric, yet user still hears tremble. Tone/loudness/vocoder instability remains a hypothesis, not an established diagnosis.\n\nOfficial Seed-VC documentation identifies the installed whisper-base F0 44.1k branch as its singing model; V2 is not a straightforward singing upgrade. Candidate longer-term routes: fine-tune a dedicated Mana singing converter on clean consistent voice material; or a DiffSinger/OpenUTAU voicebank for score-driven pitch/expression control, requiring a separate synthesis/data workflow. RVC/Applio and a legacy Mana voice checkpoint already exist locally, but that checkpoint must not be presented as the current approved voice or silently installed. No new models downloaded and no production audio settings changed in this diagnostic turn.\n\nPrimary sources: https://github.com/Plachtaa/seed-vc ; https://github.com/RVC-Project/Retrieval-based-Voice-Conversion-WebUI ; https://github.com/openvpi/DiffSinger .\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
